00:48:40.426 --> 00:48:42.842
they filter information from

00:48:42.842 --> 00:48:43.702
the environment.

00:48:45.222 --> 00:48:47.322
Because infants bodies and skills develop,

00:48:47.702 --> 00:48:50.112
that means the environment also

00:48:50.352 --> 00:48:52.342
develops. And that means

00:48:52.902 --> 00:48:55.142
that across development, infants

00:48:55.142 --> 00:48:56.972
in the same environment do not

00:48:57.432 --> 00:48:59.432
experience the same environment.

00:49:02.642 --> 00:49:03.622
Number two,

00:49:05.281 --> 00:49:07.722
self generated. Alright?

00:49:08.452 --> 00:49:10.482
But then, what motivates infants to

00:49:10.482 --> 00:49:12.722
generate all that Why do

00:49:12.722 --> 00:49:13.382
they move?

00:49:14.992 --> 00:49:17.262
So One common sense hypothesis

00:49:17.262 --> 00:49:19.501
is that infants move to

00:49:19.501 --> 00:49:21.582
get to the people and places and things that

00:49:21.582 --> 00:49:23.971
they see. So, to study

00:49:23.972 --> 00:49:25.752
whether where infants look

00:49:26.122 --> 00:49:27.822
influences where they go,

00:49:28.412 --> 00:49:30.832
we fitted them with head mounted eye trackers.

00:49:32.372 --> 00:49:34.392
If infants really move

00:49:35.052 --> 00:49:37.222
to go to destination, then they should

00:49:37.222 --> 00:49:39.452
look at something while they're stationary and then

00:49:39.452 --> 00:49:41.461
go to it. So here's what that would

00:49:41.462 --> 00:49:43.037
look like. That baby

00:49:43.602 --> 00:49:46.022
sees the ball and then walks

00:49:46.082 --> 00:49:48.062
straight to the ball and gets

00:49:50.142 --> 00:49:52.332
But it turns out those kinds

00:49:52.332 --> 00:49:54.722
of destination directed bouts are

00:49:54.722 --> 00:49:55.757
pretty rare.

00:49:57.632 --> 00:49:59.972
It's also possible that babies

00:50:00.032 --> 00:50:02.072
discover something while they're traveling.

00:50:02.811 --> 00:50:05.072
So in a discovery doubt, infants

00:50:05.322 --> 00:50:07.561
start out looking at whatever. They see

00:50:07.561 --> 00:50:09.292
things like maybe that's sucks

00:50:10.222 --> 00:50:11.932
and then they'll see something else like

00:50:12.412 --> 00:50:14.602
the green alligator. And then that becomes

00:50:14.602 --> 00:50:16.242
like a found goal.

00:50:18.482 --> 00:50:20.422
Discovery bounce are also rare.

00:50:21.642 --> 00:50:23.502
What's happening most of the time?

00:50:24.382 --> 00:50:26.882
Well, babies are standing there looking around

00:50:26.942 --> 00:50:29.002
and then they start moving and

00:50:29.002 --> 00:50:30.912
there's still looking around,

00:50:31.212 --> 00:50:32.832
and then they'll just stop

00:50:33.292 --> 00:50:35.032
moving in the middle of the room.

00:50:35.592 --> 00:50:37.772
Beyond arm's reach of any recognizable

00:50:38.607 --> 00:50:40.362
person place, or thing.

00:50:42.122 --> 00:50:44.242
Most of babies bounce don't

00:50:44.457 --> 00:50:46.462
involve a destination at

00:50:46.462 --> 00:50:46.892
all.

00:50:48.732 --> 00:50:50.972
So we figured if it were really

00:50:50.972 --> 00:50:53.052
true, that objects like toys are

00:50:53.052 --> 00:50:55.392
not needed to instigate low commotion,

00:50:56.422 --> 00:50:58.452
then infants should move just as

00:50:58.452 --> 00:51:00.302
much in a totally empty room

00:51:00.542 --> 00:51:02.602
as in a room filled with toys.

00:51:04.541 --> 00:51:06.801
We find infants walk just

00:51:06.942 --> 00:51:09.042
as much in an empty room as

00:51:09.042 --> 00:51:11.402
in a toy filled room, They spend

00:51:11.722 --> 00:51:13.582
the same amount of time in motion,

00:51:14.942 --> 00:51:17.037
they take the same number of steps per

00:51:17.037 --> 00:51:19.422
hour and they travel the same

00:51:19.422 --> 00:51:20.902
distance per hour.

00:51:22.352 --> 00:51:24.132
And infants in both conditions

00:51:24.622 --> 00:51:26.912
go to the same low percentage

00:51:26.972 --> 00:51:29.102
of destination. Only

00:51:29.102 --> 00:51:31.172
thirty percent. In the toy

00:51:31.632 --> 00:51:33.612
room, infants mostly went to toys, In

00:51:33.672 --> 00:51:35.831
the empty room, infants went to their

00:51:35.832 --> 00:51:37.852
caregivers and to features of the

00:51:37.852 --> 00:51:40.262
room. Seventy

00:51:40.402 --> 00:51:42.482
percent of the time, babies are just

00:51:42.482 --> 00:51:43.371
running around.

00:51:45.372 --> 00:51:47.692
What differs is that infants

00:51:47.692 --> 00:51:49.861
