00:52:12.682 --> 00:52:14.922
So how can we explain

00:52:14.982 --> 00:52:17.092
baby exploration? The

00:52:17.092 --> 00:52:19.272
classic optimal foraging model

00:52:20.082 --> 00:52:21.602
proposes that agents balance

00:52:22.487 --> 00:52:24.502
for moving, like a toy,

00:52:25.461 --> 00:52:27.621
against the cost of moving, the effort cost of

00:52:27.622 --> 00:52:29.811
moving. So, optimal

00:52:29.952 --> 00:52:32.132
foraging treats babies as

00:52:32.192 --> 00:52:33.962
if they're rational explorers.

00:52:35.882 --> 00:52:37.962
But the optimal foraging model

00:52:37.962 --> 00:52:39.832
cannot explain baby x

00:52:40.231 --> 00:52:42.011
exploration. Infants are not fully

00:52:42.311 --> 00:52:44.662
rational explorers. The simulated

00:52:44.882 --> 00:52:46.962
agents fail to move at all and the no

00:52:46.962 --> 00:52:49.152
toy room where infants didn't

00:52:49.152 --> 00:52:51.372
have toys to go to as a reward.

00:52:52.332 --> 00:52:54.652
Infants don't expend energy only

00:52:54.652 --> 00:52:56.792
to get to x external reward.

00:52:58.712 --> 00:53:01.021
We tested the effect of

00:53:01.021 --> 00:53:02.621
adding an internal reward

00:53:03.182 --> 00:53:05.002
to the optimal foraging model

00:53:05.882 --> 00:53:08.202
So here, babies are weighing the cost

00:53:08.202 --> 00:53:10.642
of moving against probability

00:53:10.942 --> 00:53:13.282
of an external reward plus getting

00:53:13.502 --> 00:53:15.221
an internal reward for moving.

00:53:16.742 --> 00:53:18.822
We called our model the

00:53:19.122 --> 00:53:21.252
frolicking forager and it

00:53:21.252 --> 00:53:23.182
leads the baby

00:53:23.742 --> 00:53:24.332
exploration data.

00:53:26.491 --> 00:53:28.991
If we remove the cost of moving,

00:53:29.322 --> 00:53:30.782
we find that a tireless

00:53:31.462 --> 00:53:32.951
feliker does not

00:53:33.752 --> 00:53:35.852
baby exploration. So babies are not

00:53:35.852 --> 00:53:37.832
just burning off surplus energy.

00:53:37.991 --> 00:53:39.871
That's not why they move so much.

00:53:41.232 --> 00:53:43.472
And only external reward but no

00:53:43.472 --> 00:53:45.742
cost like a sort of tireless

00:53:46.252 --> 00:53:48.602
forager. Cannot explain. Infinite

00:53:49.067 --> 00:53:50.482
exploration. So babies

00:53:51.162 --> 00:53:53.492
are not motivated solely to exploit

00:53:54.132 --> 00:53:54.802
external rewards.

00:53:57.122 --> 00:53:59.062
Finally, we used our models

00:53:59.202 --> 00:54:01.412
to test the nature of the

00:54:01.412 --> 00:54:03.722
internal reward. We

00:54:03.722 --> 00:54:05.962
find that infants are not moving just

00:54:05.962 --> 00:54:07.787
to burn off surplus energy,

00:54:08.582 --> 00:54:10.782
and rewarding the model

00:54:10.892 --> 00:54:13.131
for moving faster. And better.

00:54:13.771 --> 00:54:16.011
Like a sort of competence motivation like babies

00:54:16.011 --> 00:54:17.802
move so much because they wanna

00:54:18.042 --> 00:54:20.062
practice walking and get better at walking.

00:54:20.152 --> 00:54:22.302
Not so. That does

00:54:22.302 --> 00:54:24.532
not am the infant data.

00:54:25.622 --> 00:54:27.762
The frolicking forager model fits

00:54:27.762 --> 00:54:29.852
best. Suggesting it

00:54:29.852 --> 00:54:31.491
just feels good to move.

00:54:35.172 --> 00:54:37.272
Movement achieves goals course, it does.

00:54:37.272 --> 00:54:39.292
But movement is also its

00:54:39.292 --> 00:54:41.427
own reward. At least for

00:54:41.427 --> 00:54:43.342
